Leetcode - 213  🏠 House Robber II


1. Problem Statement

You have houses arranged in a circle.

Each house contains some money.

You want to rob houses and get the maximum amount of money, but:

You cannot rob two adjacent houses.

Because the houses are circular, the first and last houses are also adjacent.

Example:

nums = [2, 7, 9, 3, 1]

You cannot rob both 2 and 1.



2. 🧠 Main Intuition

same as like house robber - I
Do dp on house robber in the range
  0 till last_index-1
  1 till last_index
return max(last_index,last_index-1)


Logic :

Since the houses are arranged in a circle, the first and last houses are adjacent, so I cannot rob both of them. Therefore, I divide the problem into two cases.

In the first case, I exclude the last house and apply the normal House Robber DP from the first house to the second-last house. In the second case, I exclude the first house and apply the same DP from the second house to the last house.

For each house, I either skip it and keep the previous maximum, or rob it and add its money to the maximum from two houses before. Finally, I take the maximum result from these two cases


Code :

public int rob(int[] nums) {
        if(nums.length==1){
            return nums[0];
        }
        if(nums.length==2){
            return Math.max(nums[0],nums[1]);
        }
        int[] dp=new int[nums.length];
        dp[0]=nums[0];
        dp[1]=Math.max(nums[0],nums[1]);
        for(int i=2;i<nums.length-1;i++){
            dp[i]=Math.max(dp[i-1],nums[i]+dp[i-2]);
        }
        nums[2]=Math.max(nums[1],nums[2]);
        for(int i=3;i<nums.length;i++){
             nums[i]=Math.max(nums[i-1],nums[i]+nums[i-2]);
        }
        return Math.max(dp[nums.length-2],nums[nums.length-1]);
    }
